      "math_academy_id": "e-13076",
      "problem": "Let $A$ and $B$ be events. Sketch a Venn diagram that shows a shaded region representing the event $A' \\cup B'.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first consider the shaded region representing $A'$ and $B'$ separately.\n\n- The event $A'$ is represented by the shaded region below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260559/assets/d0b8d298adbec56cf806ddac183e1865bc2908d0fbf75b1935030d491d839850.png)\n\n- The event $B'$ is represented by the shaded region below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260559/assets/c7b8767c53739f3f44cc99eee7d1cc24621ab346247c083e9624f8a10fc512e2.png)\n\nFinally, $A' \\cup B'$ is the union of the two shaded regions shown above: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14260559/assets/6cd7efdce23e23882ba6ece09c6f41c67c3678846608491a7ed83bc17c103bf2.png)",
